
Zendure zenSDK Proxy - Zendure-zenSDK-proxy (gast777)
Copyright (c) 2026 Casper Rijnders

Modification notice for abaart/Zendure-zenSDK-proxy:

This fork adds an AppDaemon/Python implementation in
apps/Zendure-zenSDK-proxy/ while preserving the original Node-RED proxy
materials from gast777/Zendure-zenSDK-proxy.

The AppDaemon/Python implementation adds these project files:

- apps/Zendure-zenSDK-proxy/zendure_proxy.py
- apps/Zendure-zenSDK-proxy/zendure_proxy_config.py
- apps/Zendure-zenSDK-proxy/zendure_proxy_device_client.py
- apps/Zendure-zenSDK-proxy/zendure_proxy_get_handler.py
- apps/Zendure-zenSDK-proxy/zendure_proxy_health.py
- apps/Zendure-zenSDK-proxy/zendure_proxy_logging.py
- apps/Zendure-zenSDK-proxy/zendure_proxy_metrics.py
- apps/Zendure-zenSDK-proxy/zendure_proxy_post_handler.py
- apps/Zendure-zenSDK-proxy/zendure_proxy_power.py
- apps/Zendure-zenSDK-proxy/zendure_proxy_queue.py
- apps/Zendure-zenSDK-proxy/zendure_proxy_standby.py
- apps/Zendure-zenSDK-proxy/zendure_proxy_state.py
- examples/apps.yaml
- hacs.json

The AppDaemon/Python implementation has three concrete goals:

- HACS installs and updates the AppDaemon app from this repository, so users do
  not need to import a Node-RED JSON export manually for the AppDaemon version.
- RequestQueue in zendure_proxy_queue.py and DeviceClient in
  zendure_proxy_device_client.py serialize and coalesce HTTP requests, so Zendure
  devices receive fewer simultaneous requests in edge-case situations.
- zendure_proxy_health.py tracks Healthy, Degraded, and Dead status per Zendure,
  so the AppDaemon/Python implementation can answer Home Assistant from cache
  and continue controlling healthy Zendures when one Zendure stops responding.
- During Degraded status, the AppDaemon/Python implementation does not send POST
  commands to the degraded Zendure, but it counts the last measured wattage from
  that Zendure for a configurable period before treating the Zendure as Dead.
- The Python modules in apps/Zendure-zenSDK-proxy/ make GitHub review and
  contribution easier than reviewing a single-line Node-RED JSON export.

The original Node-RED implementation from gast777/Zendure-zenSDK-proxy remains
unchanged by these AppDaemon/Python additions.

